## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical firewall configuration skills on RHEL 9, requiring precise rule creation, persistence, and verification—essential for enterprise security administration.

## Key Concepts
- nftables ruleset syntax and packet flow
- Rule persistence via /etc/nftables.conf
- Service management with systemctl
- Connectivity testing from allowed vs. disallowed sources
- Verification using nft list ruleset

## Code Example
```bash
#!/usr/sbin/nft -f
flush ruleset
table inet filter {
  chain input {
    type filter hook input priority 0; policy drop;
    iifname "lo" accept
    ip saddr 192.168.1.0/24 tcp dport 22 accept
  }
  chain forward {
    type filter hook forward priority 0; policy drop;
  }
  chain output {
    type filter hook output priority 0; policy accept;
  }
}
```

## Implementation Steps
```bash
# Install nftables
dnf install -y nftables

# Create ruleset
cat > /etc/nftables.conf << 'EOF'
#!/usr/sbin/nft -f
flush ruleset
table inet filter {
  chain input {
    type filter hook input priority 0; policy drop;
    iifname "lo" accept
    ip saddr 192.168.1.0/24 tcp dport 22 accept
  }
  chain forward {
    type filter hook forward priority 0; policy drop;
  }
  chain output {
    type filter hook output priority 0; policy accept;
  }
}
EOF

# Enable and start services
systemctl enable nftables
systemctl start nftables
systemctl status nftables

# Verify rules
nft list ruleset

# Test connectivity (from allowed host)
ssh user@server-ip

# Test connectivity (from disallowed host)
ssh user@server-ip  # Should timeout/refuse
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to build a multi-tenant TLS termination with live updates in a containerized RH9 setup, including security and networking constraints.

## Key Concepts
- TLS with SNI and per-tenant certs
- Podman container networking
- Local CA management and cert rotation
- systemd-based zero-downtime reloads
- SELinux policy and nftables isolation
- End-to-end test planning

## Code Example
```javascript
// watcher: rotate tenant certs and reload proxy
const fs = require('fs');
const { execSync } = require('child_process');
const watchDir = '/var/lib/proxy/certs';
const watcher = require('chokidar').watch(watchDir);
watcher.on('change', (path) => {
  if (path.endsWith('.pem')) {
    fs.copyFileSync(`${watchDir}/current.pem`, '/var/run/proxy/current.pem.bak');
    execSync('systemctl reload rhproxy');
  }
});
```

